      <h2>Where Killeen parties actually fit</h2>
      <p>
        Most driveway birthdays land in neighborhoods off W.S. Young, Trimmier, and Stan Schlueter. A cul-de-sac can look wide until the truck and the trailer are in a line. Plan on about 50–60 feet of level frontage, clear of low branches and basketball goals, until the measured length of this rig replaces that range. Newer streets in south Killeen and over the line in Harker Heights are the same problem: pretty curb, short straight.
      </p>
      <p>
        Apartments along the US-190 corridor, and complexes near Killeen Mall, need a yes from the office before the trailer rolls in. A clubhouse reservation is not permission to park a trailer on their asphalt. Send the written okay with the booking so the coach is not arguing with a courtesy officer at the gate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Public parks and the grounds around the Killeen Civic and Conference Center follow City of Killeen rules. Reserve the park with the city, then reserve the trailer. We do not book pavilions for you, and we do not assume a splash-pad crowd leaves a level pad big enough for the rig.
      </p>
      <p>
        Skylark Field, the Killeen–Fort Cavazos Regional Airport, is a useful pin when you are texting a cross street. It is not a setup site. Give a street address the tow vehicle can legally stop at. Airside is not it.
      </p>
